<BaseLayout title="About Dama Workshop" description="How Dama Workshop builds, checks and maintains its free woodworking calculators and practical measurement guides." activeNav="/about/">
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--about"><div class="shell page-hero__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">About Dama Workshop</p><h1>Arithmetic you can inspect.</h1></div><p>Dama Workshop is an independent calculator library for hobby woodworkers and small shops. It exists to answer a measurement question quickly without hiding the formula or pretending a digital result replaces physical verification.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section section--paper"><div class="shell about-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our purpose</p><h2>Make repetitive shop math easier to trust.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Plans mix decimal dimensions, tape-measure fractions, hardware clearances and material-pricing conventions. A generic calculator can perform arithmetic, but it rarely explains which measurement belongs in the box or where the result stops being reliable.</p><p>Dama Workshop combines each calculator with a plain-language method, worked example, rounding choice and limitation. Inputs are processed locally in the browser. No account is required and measurements are not sent to our server.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell principles-grid"><article><span>01</span><h2>Formula first</h2><p>Every calculator states the core relationship it uses. Results should be reproducible with a pencil or another calculator.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h2>Assumptions visible</h2><p>Joinery type, kerf treatment, reveal and waste allowance are exposed instead of silently built into a result.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h2>No invented testing</h2><p>We distinguish established shop math from physical testing and never present generated examples as personal workshop experience.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h2>Corrections welcomed</h2><p>Ambiguous labels, arithmetic errors and accessibility problems can be reported through the public correction channel.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="section section--dark"><div class="shell standards-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Editorial standard</p><h2>What we check before publishing</h2><p><a class="text-link text-link--light" href="/standards/">Read the complete standard →</a></p></div><ul class="check-list check-list--light"><li>Default examples calculate correctly</li><li>Mixed fractions reduce correctly</li><li>Invalid physical dimensions return a useful error</li><li>Formula, explanation and code agree</li><li>Every local link resolves in the production build</li><li>Mobile inputs remain usable without horizontal scrolling</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell about-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ownership & funding</p><h2>Independent and free to use.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Dama Workshop is operated as an independent web property. The site may display clearly identified advertising after the required consent and policy controls are implemented. Advertising does not change calculator outputs or editorial conclusions.</p><p>Current calculator pages do not contain paid product rankings, sponsored claims or affiliate recommendations. Any future commercial relationship will be disclosed where it appears.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Report a correction or contact the publisher →</a></p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
